      "id": "claim_39e0eb0db55e4b64a058657d1195784a",
      "statement": "Despite the Aurora PostgreSQL datastore shown in Trusted Actions' architecture diagram, Phase-2 placeholder variables (db_username, db_name), and now-live (uncommented) Phase-2 scaffold security groups for a future Fargate ecs_task and for Aurora inbound Postgres access in terraform/regional/security_groups.tf, the currently applied regional Terraform runs SQLiteStore in production: the ECS task definition hardcodes DATABASE_URL to the file-backed path /data/trusted_actions.db mounted from a dedicated encrypted EBS volume attached to a single EC2 host, the ALB target group remains target_type = \"instance\" rather than Fargate awsvpc networking, and no aurora.tf file or aws_rds_cluster/Aurora resource of any kind exists in the regional root yet despite the aurora security group's comment claiming one is referenced.",
