    {
      "id": "claim_07b78db195d44015ab3dc294a67f1d16",
      "statement": "terraform/regional/ecs.tf's locals.compat_env computes ECS environment-variable values for eight settings (worker concurrency/poll-interval/execution-timeout, allowed namespaces/secrets, OCM base URL, Backplane URL/client ID) by preferring the corresponding deprecated per-setting Terraform variable when it is explicitly set (non-null), and otherwise falling back to the matching key decoded from the app_config YAML via try(...); a setting absent from both sources yields an empty string and container_environment's `if value != \"\"` filter then omits that environment entry entirely. terraform/regional/variables.tf documents this as a one-release compatibility shim: it lets an old deployed container image, which reads only ROSA_TA_* environment variables and has no config-file support for backplane/ocm/workers/allowlists settings, and a new image, which reads those settings from the mounted config.yaml, both receive consistent effective configuration from the same Terraform apply, because the Go config loader's env-over-file precedence makes an env value equal to the file value harmless for the new image while remaining authoritative for the old one; the code comments on both the deprecated variables and the compat_env/container_environment merge state they are to be removed in a future change once the old image is fully retired.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/terraform/regional/ecs.tf#L10-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:da74245cc4aada1b86446c4fca1a68a2f3d64ad875693115518d9db8a7cb5790:"
        },
        {
